quran[24]{c,v,t}:
  37,103,"So when they both submitted (to Allah’s will) and he laid him on his forehead (for sacrifice),"
  37,104,We called out to him: ‘O Ibrahim (Abraham)!
  37,105,"You have fulfilled the dream!’ Indeed, this is how We reward the virtuously excellent!"
  37,106,"Most surely, this was a manifest trial."
  37,107,Then We ransomed him with a great sacrifice.
  37,108,And We left for him (an honourable mention) among later generations.
  37,109,Peace be upon Ibrahim (Abraham)!
  37,110,That is how We reward the virtuously excellent.
  37,111,"Surely, he was among Our faithful servants."
  37,112,Then We gave him glad tidings of (the birth of another son) Ishaq (Isaac)—a prophet (and) one of the righteous.
  37,113,"And We bestowed blessings upon him and Ishaq (Isaac). And among their descendants, (some) are virtuous and (some) who openly wrong themselves."
  37,114,"And indeed, We conferred favour upon Musa (Moses) and Harun (Aaron)."
  37,115,And We saved them and their people from great distress.
  37,116,"And We helped them, so they were the ones who became the victors."
  37,117,"We gave the two of them the clarifying Book (i.e. the Torah),"
  37,118,and guided them both to the straight path.
  37,119,And We left for them (an honourable mention) among the later generations.
  37,120,Peace be upon Musa (Moses) and Harun (Aaron)!
  37,121,"Indeed, this is how We reward the virtuously excellent."
  37,122,"Surely, they both were among Our faithful servants."
  37,123,"And indeed, Ilyas (Elias) was one of the messengers."
  37,124,When he said to his people: ‘Will you not be God-conscious?
  37,125,"Do you worship (the idol) Ba‘l and leave the best of the creators,"
  37,126,"Allah, your Lord and the Lord of your forefathers?’"
